MOST ASKED INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
=========================================================

Q1. What is Encapsulation?

Wrapping data and methods together into a class while restricting direct access to the internal data.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q2. What is Abstraction?

Hiding implementation details while exposing only essential functionality.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q3. Difference between Encapsulation and Abstraction?

Encapsulation hides DATA.

Abstraction hides IMPLEMENTATION.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q4. What is Inheritance?

A mechanism where a derived class acquires properties and behavior of a base class.

Represents an IS-A relationship.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q5. What is Polymorphism?

One interface with multiple implementations.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q6. Difference between Compile-Time and Runtime Polymorphism?

Compile-Time
• Function Overloading
• Operator Overloading
• Templates

Runtime
• Virtual Functions
• Function Overriding

---------------------------------------------------------

Q7. How is Runtime Polymorphism Implemented in C++?

Using virtual functions.

Compiler creates
• vtable (Virtual Table)

Each object stores
• vptr (Virtual Pointer)

During runtime, the vptr points to the correct overridden function, enabling dynamic dispatch.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q8. Why Prefer Composition Over Inheritance?

Because composition provides:

• Low coupling
• High cohesion
• Better maintainability
• Better flexibility
• Easy testing
• Components can be replaced independently

Prefer Composition unless there is a genuine IS-A relationship.

